  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="31">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIIIAtr">VIII Atr</ref> 31</head>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="31" corresp="#wit-d">Ac we lærað georne ⁊ luflice biddað, þæt ælces hades men þam life libban þe heom to gebirige.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-d">But we earnestly enjoin and, with all good-will, beg men of every estate to live such a life as befits them.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Sondern wir weisen ernstlich an und bitten freundschaftlich, dass Menschen jeden Standes in solcher Lebensweise leben, welche ihnen gebührt.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">But we earnestly instruct and lovingly ask that people of every order live the life that befits them.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Liebermann compares VI Atr 2.1.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
